{"id":"leetcode-250","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Count Univalue Subtrees","summary":"Determine the count of univalued subtrees within a binary tree.","statement":"Determine the count of univalued subtrees within a binary tree. A univalued subtree consists of nodes with identical values.","constraints":["0–1000 nodes; values range from -1000 to 1000. The binary tree may be sparse or skewed.","A subtree consists of a node and ALL of its descendants. Count it if every value equals its root value. Every leaf counts; a connected same-value portion of a nonuniform subtree does not count."],"topics":["trees","recursion","dynamic-programming"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"count_univalue_subtrees","parameters":[{"name":"root","annotation":"TreeNode | None","adapter":"treenode","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"int","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"# Data structure supplied to this problem.\nclass TreeNode:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        val: int = 0,\n        left: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n        right: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n    ):\n        self.val = val\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\n\ndef count_univalue_subtrees(root: TreeNode | None) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def count_univalue_subtrees(root):\n    uniform, result = {}, 0\n    stack = [(root, False)]\n    while stack:\n        node, visited = stack.pop()\n        if node is None:\n            continue\n        if not visited:\n            stack.extend(((node, True), (node.right, False), (node.left, False)))\n            continue\n        same = all(child is None or (uniform[id(child)] and child.val == node.val)\n                   for child in (node.left, node.right))\n        uniform[id(node)] = same\n        result += same\n    return result\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def count_univalue_subtrees(root):\n    stack, result = [root], 0\n    while stack:\n        node = stack.pop()\n        if node is not None:\n            result += node.left is None and node.right is None\n            stack.extend((node.left, node.right))\n    return result\n","def count_univalue_subtrees(root):\n    uniform, result = {}, 0\n    stack = [(root, False)]\n    while stack:\n        node, visited = stack.pop()\n        if node is None:\n            continue\n        if not visited:\n            stack.extend(((node, True), (node.right, False), (node.left, False)))\n            continue\n        same = all(child is None or child.val == node.val\n                   for child in (node.left, node.right))\n        uniform[id(node)] = same\n        result += same\n    return result\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(n)","estimated_minutes":35,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":2,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["A parent subtree can be uniform only if each of its child subtrees is already uniform.","Process children before their parent and retain one uniform/nonuniform result per child.","A node qualifies when each existing child is uniform and has the node's value; add one for each qualifying node.","Use explicit postorder frames for a 1000-node chain, preserving recursive dependencies without relying on the interpreter's recursion limit."],"editorial":"Uniformity is a postorder property: both child subtrees must be uniform, and their root values must match the parent. Every qualifying node contributes one subtree, including internal nodes and leaves. An explicit visited-frame stack evaluates each node after its children and avoids deep-call-stack errors. The independent oracle stores binary paths and, for each possible subtree root, directly scans all descendant values. Tests distinguish an entire subtree from a partial same-value region and include both uniformly valued and nonuniform deep structures.","tests":[{"id":"lc-250-1","arguments":[[5,1,5,5,5,null,5]],"expected":4,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The three leaves each count, and the right child 5 with its leaf 5 counts too. The subtree rooted at 1 and the entire tree are not uniform, so the total is 4.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-2","arguments":[[]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"There are no node-rooted subtrees in an empty tree, so the answer is 0.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-3","arguments":[[1]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-4","arguments":[[1,1]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-5","arguments":[[1,2]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-6","arguments":[[1,1,1]],"expected":3,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-7","arguments":[[1,1,1,2]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-8","arguments":[[5,5,5,5,5,null,5]],"expected":6,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-9","arguments":[[0,-1,0]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-10","arguments":[[-1000]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-11","arguments":[[1000,1000,1000]],"expected":3,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-12","arguments":[[1,null,1,null,2]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-250-13","arguments":[[2,2,null,2]],"expected":3,"comparator